In Brazil, we have witnessed how concentrated media ownership can lead to an echo chamber, where only certain perspectives are amplified. Public funding, when properly managed and transparent, can be a way to support independent media that might not otherwise survive economically. It ensures that a variety of viewpoints reach the population, fostering a more democratic and informed citizenry. 

